  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/dom.html#the-dir-attribute\n\n> Can be set, to either \"ltr\", \"rtl\", or \"auto\" to replace the html element's dir attribute's value.\n\nThis does not clearly indicate what happens if the value is set to something other than the enumerated values.  The implication is that the rules for reflected IDL attributes are followed, which perform the attribute set on the underlying element -- but (at least one version of) the HTMLWG test cases expects the attribute to be removed entirely if `document.dir = '';` is executed.  It may be worth clarifying the behavior in this case.\n",
